    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as the clear anchor of our offense, leading the team with an elite 85.94 score. The combination of a favorable matchup against the vulnerable arm of Tomoyuki Sugano (5.02 xERA) and the high-leverage spot in the #2 hole makes him a must-start; he is the primary engine for our team\u2019s stolen base production. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Tyler Soderstrom**, who benefits significantly from a high-park-factor environment and a soft matchup against Nick Martinez, pushing his score to an impressive 72.72. **Gabriel Moreno** also provides excellent value (71.17) as his refined xwOBA and the presumed order advantage against Sugano solidify his spot behind the plate.\n\nThe optimization process was tightest regarding the bottom of the order, where **Jose Caballero** (46.23) and **Austin Riley** (46.88) narrowly held off **Zach McKinstry** (43.02) and **Travis Bazzana** (41.97). While **Zach McKinstry** offered potential, a poor BvP history and a deep position in the batting order ultimately cratered his floor, keeping him on the bench. We are wary of **Cole Young** and **Josh Naylor** facing Ryan Weathers; despite the decent park factors, the elite-adjacent nature of Weathers\u2019 3.41 xERA dragged their scores into the marginal range. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our depth pieces like **Mickey Moniak**, who carries risk due to a negative platoon split against lefty Mitch Bratt but remains active for his overall lineup slot utility. \n\nAll starters are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status, which introduces volatility to the projected order advantages. Be advised that any shifts in batting position\u2014particularly for **Brice Turang** at the leadoff spot or **Max Muncy** down at #8\u2014could necessitate a shift in confidence levels if late-breaking news alters their run-scoring opportunities. We remain fully committed to maximizing our stolen base upside today, prioritizing speed over pure power in marginal lineup spots.",
